.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt CALL 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm call
.Nd typed RPC call on a scheme-file handle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x67).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends an opaque request of
.Fa request_len
bytes with an optional response buffer of
.Fa response_len
bytes to the server owning a scheme-file handle, and blocks until the server replies.
It returns the number of response bytes the server reported.
The request and response ranges are captured as kernel-owned copies; the server addresses in
the packet point at those copies, never at the client's pages
.Pq see Pa docs/design/capture.md .
The request capture is read-only for the server; the response capture is writable.
On completion the kernel copies the response back to the client only if the client's mapping is
still the one captured at request time.
.Pp
A successful reply may report at most
.Fa response_len
bytes; a larger result is a protocol violation and the call returns
.Er EPROTO ,
never a silently clamped length.
Zero-length and exactly-at-capacity replies are valid.
.Pp
If the server exits while the call is pending, the call returns
.Er EIO .
The kernel releases the captured frames after the server has retired the request; a server
still touching a cancelled capture sees kernel-owned memory, not a recycled client frame.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The reported response length on success.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EIO
The server died before replying.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
The reply was malformed or reported more than the response capacity.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A request or response range is not mapped, or a writable response range is read-only.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr send 2 ,
.Xr recv 2 ,
.Xr open 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
